WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.013
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B two, Book two.

2
00:00:05.313 --> 00:00:08.770
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:16.006
Unit twenty-four: Health Misinformation. Today you will report claims and facts with reported speech.

4
00:00:16.306 --> 00:00:18.947
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:23.353
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.217 --> 00:00:25.531
Misinformation.

7
00:00:26.517 --> 00:00:29.584
Misinformation means false information that spreads.

8
00:00:30.183 --> 00:00:32.566
Health misinformation can be dangerous.

9
00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:35.907
Your turn. Say: Misinformation.

10
00:00:38.767 --> 00:00:40.104
Misinformation.

11
00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:41.630
Myth.

12
00:00:42.617 --> 00:00:45.359
Myth means a popular belief that is not true.

13
00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:48.449
It's a myth that cold weather causes colds.

14
00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:51.679
Your turn. Say: Myth.

15
00:00:54.533 --> 00:00:55.209
Myth.

16
00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:56.835
Evidence.

17
00:00:57.850 --> 00:01:00.128
Evidence means facts that prove something.

18
00:01:00.717 --> 00:01:02.600
There is no evidence for that claim.

19
00:01:03.217 --> 00:01:05.881
Your turn. Say: Evidence.

20
00:01:08.733 --> 00:01:09.862
Evidence.

21
00:01:10.617 --> 00:01:11.687
Source.

22
00:01:12.683 --> 00:01:15.159
Source means where information comes from.

23
00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:17.668
Check the source before you share.

24
00:01:18.283 --> 00:01:20.750
Your turn. Say: Source.

25
00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:24.555
Source.

26
00:01:25.317 --> 00:01:26.306
Expert.

27
00:01:27.317 --> 00:01:29.897
Expert means a person with special knowledge.

28
00:01:30.483 --> 00:01:32.611
Ask an expert, like a doctor.

29
00:01:33.217 --> 00:01:35.846
Your turn. Say: Expert.

30
00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:39.748
Expert.

31
00:01:40.483 --> 00:01:41.264
Viral.

32
00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:44.760
Viral means spreading very fast online.

33
00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:47.013
The fake video went viral.

34
00:01:47.617 --> 00:01:50.165
Your turn. Say: Viral.

35
00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:53.908
Viral.

36
00:01:54.650 --> 00:01:55.674
Fact-check.

37
00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:59.728
Fact-check means to check if something is true.

38
00:02:00.317 --> 00:02:02.502
Always fact-check health tips.

39
00:02:03.117 --> 00:02:05.990
Your turn. Say: Fact-check.

40
00:02:08.833 --> 00:02:09.834
Fact-check.

41
00:02:10.583 --> 00:02:11.306
Trust.

42
00:02:12.317 --> 00:02:14.885
Trust means believing that someone is honest.

43
00:02:15.483 --> 00:02:17.506
Doctors earn our trust with evidence.

44
00:02:18.117 --> 00:02:20.572
Your turn. Say: Trust.

45
00:02:23.433 --> 00:02:24.098
Trust.

46
00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:28.237
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:29.083 --> 00:02:32.627
Visal, did you see the viral post about lemon water curing flu?

48
00:02:33.717 --> 00:02:38.296
Yes, but I asked a doctor. The doctor said that the claim was false.

49
00:02:39.383 --> 00:02:41.000
What else did she say?

50
00:02:42.083 --> 00:02:45.128
She told me that there was no evidence for it.

51
00:02:46.217 --> 00:02:47.253
Good thinking!

52
00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:52.300
My teacher said that we should always fact-check health tips.

53
00:02:53.467 --> 00:02:55.130
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:55.983 --> 00:02:58.412
Grammar focus: Reported speech.

55
00:02:58.712 --> 00:02:59.888
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:00.583 --> 00:03:02.745
The doctor said that the claim was false.

57
00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:05.673
She told me that there was no evidence.

58
00:03:06.583 --> 00:03:09.152
The expert said that the post had gone viral.

59
00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:16.894
In reported speech, the tense usually moves back: is → was, has → had, will → would.

60
00:03:17.650 --> 00:03:22.322
Be careful! Don't say: The doctor said that the claim is false yesterday.

61
00:03:24.267 --> 00:03:27.334
Say: The doctor said that the claim was false.

62
00:03:27.634 --> 00:03:31.224
In reported speech, move the tense back: is → was.

63
00:03:32.033 --> 00:03:34.628
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:35.433 --> 00:03:36.934
Check Before You Share.

65
00:03:37.234 --> 00:03:40.603
Health misinformation spreads fast when posts go viral.

66
00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:43.832
Many popular tips are just myths.

67
00:03:44.833 --> 00:03:47.797
A doctor said that one viral cure was dangerous.

68
00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:51.531
Experts told us that we should check the source.

69
00:03:52.533 --> 00:03:55.775
If you fact-check, you protect people's trust and health.

70
00:03:56.867 --> 00:04:00.601
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:03.879
The doctor said that the claim blank false.

72
00:04:04.179 --> 00:04:07.380
A, was. B, is being. C, be.

73
00:04:10.933 --> 00:04:12.794
The answer is A: was.

74
00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:16.669
A popular belief that is not true is a blank.

75
00:04:16.969 --> 00:04:20.367
A, myth. B, source. C, fact.

76
00:04:23.933 --> 00:04:25.573
The answer is A: myth.

77
00:04:26.717 --> 00:04:29.436
Spreading very fast online means blank.

78
00:04:29.736 --> 00:04:33.204
A, viral. B, expert. C, trusted.

79
00:04:36.767 --> 00:04:38.534
The answer is A: viral.

80
00:04:39.733 --> 00:04:43.024
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:04:43.883 --> 00:04:46.115
How can you spot health misinformation?

82
00:04:54.917 --> 00:04:56.487
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:04:56.787 --> 00:05:08.228
I check the source and look for evidence. Last month, my doctor said that a viral cure was fake, so now I always fact-check before I share.

84
00:05:08.528 --> 00:05:10.307
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:05:11.217 --> 00:05:15.053
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and reported speech.

86
00:05:15.353 --> 00:05:19.608
Today's value is truthfulness. Tell the truth and check the facts.

87
00:05:19.908 --> 00:05:22.607
See you in Unit twenty-five. Goodbye!

88
00:05:22.907 --> 00:05:26.221
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

